{
  "code": "CE-BS",
  "reviewed": "2026-10-23",
  "summary": "Every course must be taken for a letter grade when that option is offered (CR grades from spring 2020 through summer 2021 still count), toward the 113 units the major needs. The audit checks 45 units of math and science, the Technology in Society course, and 68 units of engineering fundamentals and depth: the core courses, programming, thermodynamics, 12 units in one depth focus area and 6 units in each of three other areas, electives as needed (at most 4 units of CEE 199/199L), and two of CEE 101A-D. You move in math and science electives from the School of Engineering lists. Honors needs the directed writing courses, a 3.3 GPA and an approved thesis.",
  "program": {
    "letterGrade": true,
    "why": "Grading: \"All courses must be taken for a letter grade, if offered.\" Other requirements: \"CR grades are acceptable only for classes completed in the six quarters between spring 2020 and summer 2021.\" The audit already accepts pass grades from those terms."
  },
  "nodes": {
